SECTION | KEY | VALUE
----------------------------------------
# office-example.plug.pdl - a LOCAL EXAMPLE plug for the pre-design book (2026-11-14). Plugs are optional and have an on/off switch: switch it in the plugs window (LyfeDesk Tools > plugs) or by editing ENABLED below.
# What it does: the example harnz `stamp this page` reads its two parameters through plug references (@plug:office-example:<key>, resolved when the harnz RUNS). Switch the plug OFF and the harnz is refused with a reason:
# the plug is what lets the harnz run. Copy this file to start your own plug; the PARAM grammar is in PLUGS-AND-HARNZ-SPEC-2026-11-14.md.
# PARAM | key | value | type | min | max | help      type: int (min and max bound it), word (letters, digits, - _), tone, text
PLUG | name | office-example
PLUG | version | 1
ENABLED | 1
AFFECTS | view
PARAM | stamp_limit | 20     | int  | 5 | 200 | how many stamp lines the harnz keeps in state/office_stamps.txt (older ones are dropped)
PARAM | stamp_label | office | word |   |     | the word written in front of each stamp line
